  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "Suppose \\(d\\) is a digit. For how many values of \\(d\\) is \\[2.00d5 > 2.005?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(6\\)",
    "E": "\\(10\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Write \\(2.005\\) as \\(2.0050\\) so both numbers show the same decimal places. In \\(2.00d5\\), the digit \\(d\\) is in the thousandths place.\n\nIf \\(d\\) is \\(0,1,2,3,\\) or \\(4\\), that place is smaller than the corresponding \\(5\\), so the inequality fails. If \\(d=5\\), then \\(2.0055>2.0050\\) because of the final decimal place. If \\(d\\) is \\(6,7,8,\\) or \\(9\\), the thousandths place already makes the number larger.\n\nThus the successful digits are \\(5,6,7,8,9\\), exactly \\(\\boxed{5}\\) values, choice \\(\\text{C}\\).",
